<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Auto Backup rules for Android 11 and below (android:fullBackupContent).

  Two things must never leave this device in a backup:

  1. beebo_prefs.xml - normally just settings, but SessionStore falls back to it
     when an OEM's keystore refuses to make a master key, and on those devices it
     holds the server bearer token and the hub JWT in the clear. A cleartext
     credential in a Google Drive backup is a credential on someone else's disk.
  2. beebo_secure.xml - the encrypted store. The ciphertext would back up, but the
     AndroidKeyStore key that decrypts it is hardware-bound and cannot. Restoring
     it onto a new phone produces an undecryptable file, not a signed-in user.

  Excluding both means a restored phone asks you to sign in again. That is the
  correct outcome, and it is what happens today anyway - just without leaving a
  copy of the token in the cloud on the way.

  offline/ is where downloaded films live. Auto Backup's quota is 25 MB; one film
  would blow past it and silently break backup for the whole app.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="beebo_prefs.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="beebo_secure.xml" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="offline/" />
</full-backup-content>
